# This directory is intentionally empty for now.
#
# It must exist: `Package.swift` declares a `JanelaDaemonTests` target, and SwiftPM
# warns about a target whose sources directory is missing.
#
# This is the highest-value test target in the project once the daemon does
# something, because the daemon's whole interface is a socket: the entire session
# lifecycle becomes testable headlessly, with no window server. Bind a real socket
# in a TemporaryDirectory, connect a test client, drive it with real messages.
#
# What belongs here (docs/testing.md § The daemon boundary):
#
#   - The client disconnects and the terminals keep running. Write this one first;
#     it is the headline promise. Start a terminal, drop the connection, reconnect,
#     assert the same pid and an intact screen.
#   - Reattach is a screen, not a replay: attach late to a terminal that has
#     produced megabytes and assert one repaint bounded by grid size.
#   - Two clients see the same screen, and the PTY is sized to the smaller viewport.
#   - Version skew refuses politely: an old handshake is rejected, the daemon stays
#     up, its terminals are untouched. Killing sessions on a version mismatch is the
#     worst bug this system can have.
#   - A peer with the wrong uid is refused.
#   - Frame boundaries: a frame split across reads, two frames in one read, a length
#     prefix past the bound, a connection that dies mid-frame.
#   - A stalled client does not stall the daemon or the other clients.
#   - Idle exit: no clients and no live terminals exits after the grace period; one
#     live terminal prevents it indefinitely.
#
# Mind `sun_path`: it is 104 bytes, and a temp directory plus a test name gets
# close. Use the short-path helper rather than building socket paths by hand, or the
# tests will pass for you and fail for someone with a longer home directory.
# See docs/decisions/0016-daemon-protocol.md.
